From 786c5caeb19bdf1c45d401ff79977cca05ad3374 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:21:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/25] Modeling Algorithms - Build a still rolling ball as a
 sphere

A ball of the radius of a concave fillet it rolls into (the start wall of
a thread over the fillet of its root) stays still there: its contact on
the other face does not move, the walked trace on that face is a point and
the approximation of the walking fails, so the whole contour fell back to
the section model. SolidWorks makes that part of the fillet a sphere.

- ChFi3d_SphereData builds a surfdata on the sphere of the ball, with its
  pole at the still contact and the trace on the other face along the
  longitude, so that the meridians through its ends are the sections of
  the neighbours. It refuses a trace that is not on the sphere (within
  max(10 tolapp3d, R/1000)).
- ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformSurf, in rolling ball mode, builds such a
  surfdata when the approximation fails on a walking whose contact on one
  face does not move, twisted on that side.
- PerformSetOfKGen rebuilds a twisted surfdata ending at a point on one
  side as the sphere instead of a filling, in rolling ball mode for a
  constant radius, when its trace on the other side is on the sphere.
- CornerOnPrevious looks for the crossing of the traces past the first
  fifth of the trace before (was its second half): a ball too large for
  the fillet of the root makes a swallowtail on the wall whose trace after
  crosses the one before far back on it. The fillet of the wall then
  builds up to radius 2 (was 1.83), with the small triangle of the wall
  that SolidWorks leaves.

With the fillets of the crests of radius 2 (as SolidWorks made them), the
fillet of the wall of radius 1 has the sphere of SolidWorks (same center,
the deviation of its faces drops from 0.016 to 1e-5), radius 2 builds with
the triangle of the wall of SolidWorks.

Tests: bugs/modalg_8 fillet_wall_profile_sphere_at_root and
fillet_wall_profile_ball_does_not_pass_root (new data file
freecad_screw_wall_profile_crest2.brep); comment of
fillet_wall_profile_over_root updated (the fillet of the root there is
0.0024 off the sphere: still a filling).

